KG42.register("rules-9c841109ff98889e2fe5ee83",{"id":"04-energy_collectives::v141-c-R001","paper":"04-energy_collectives","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R001","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Local market clearing","process_stage":"clearing","market_meaning":"The ADMM implementation of community clearing requires a supervisory node. Scope: Community economic dispatch implemented with ADMM. Condition: ADMM is used to solve the community dispatch. The community manager directly influences the collective members' energy dispatch. Scope: Energy allocation in the proposed collective's economic dispatch. Community allocations must satisfy each prosumer's power balance and feasible net production, zero aggregate internal exchange, equality of aggregate imports and exports to their respective individual totals, and nonnegative individual imports and exports. Scope: Community dispatch exchange problem (1), including its external import and export balances. Every agent must reveal its utility curves in the central optimization problem. Scope: Centralized optimization formulation of community clearing. Condition: The central optimization formulation is used. The community market is cleared over 24 hours in a single optimization problem because of the daily consumption constraint. Scope: The paper's simulated energy collective with fixed cumulative daily consumption. Condition: Each prosumer's cumulative daily energy consumption is fixed to match the reference dataset.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function clearing.local under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["clearing.local","coordination.local_operator"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R001-E001","source":"clearing.local","target":"coordination.local_operator","type":"requires","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R001-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E31","v141-b-g01-E32"]},{"edge_id":"v141-c-R001-E002","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"clearing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R001-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e35"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Centralized optimization formulation of community clearing. | Community dispatch exchange problem (1), including its external import and export balances. | Community economic dispatch implemented with ADMM. | Energy allocation in the proposed collective's economic dispatch. | The paper's simulated energy collective with fixed cumulative daily consumption.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E17","v141-b-g01-E31","v141-b-g01-E32","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e35"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R001-X001","symbol":"p_j","meaning":"Net energy produced by prosumer j; component of the clearing decision set Gamma = {p_j, q_j, alpha_j, beta_j} of exchange problem (1).","kind":"operational","domain":"p_j in P_j (feasible space of p_j as defined by the source; P_j is not enumerated in the supplied evidence), j = 1, ..., n","unit":null,"indices":["j"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E02"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R001-X002","symbol":"q_j","meaning":"Energy imported by prosumer j from the community (internal exchange); component of the clearing decision set Gamma.","kind":"operational","domain":"real; no individual bound is stated in (1), it is constrained only in aggregate by sum_{j=1}^{n} q_j = 0","unit":null,"indices":["j"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g01-E02"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R001-X003","symbol":"α_j","meaning":"Energy imported by prosumer j from outside the community (with the market and system operator); component of the clearing decision set Gamma.","kind":"operational","domain":"α_j >= 0, j = 1, ..., n","unit":null,"indices":["j"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g01-E02"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R001-X004","symbol":"β_j","meaning":"Energy exported by prosumer j (to outside the community); component of the clearing decision set Gamma.","kind":"operational","domain":"β_j >= 0, j = 1, ..., n","unit":null,"indices":["j"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g01-E02"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R001-X005","symbol":"q_imp","meaning":"Total energy imported by the community; continuous variable describing the import exchange of the collective with the system operator, equal to sum_{j=1}^{n} α_j.","kind":"operational","domain":"continuous variable; determined by the balance sum_{j=1}^{n} α_j = q_imp (no separate bound is stated in (1))","unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E02"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R001-X006","symbol":"q_exp","meaning":"Total energy exported by the community; continuous variable describing the export exchange of the collective with the system operator, equal to sum_{j=1}^{n} β_j.","kind":"operational","domain":"continuous variable; determined by the balance sum_{j=1}^{n} β_j = q_exp (no separate bound is stated in (1))","unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E02"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R001-P001","symbol":"n","meaning":"Number of prosumers in the collective; fixed input that indexes the prosumers j = 1, ..., n in the clearing constraints (1b)-(1g).","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E02"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C001","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"The ADMM implementation of community clearing requires a supervisory node. Scope: Community economic dispatch implemented with ADMM. Condition: ADMM is used to solve the community dispatch.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local","coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E31","v141-b-g01-E32"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The community manager directly influences the collective members' energy dispatch. Scope: Energy allocation in the proposed collective's economic dispatch.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e35"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C003","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Community allocations must satisfy each prosumer's power balance and feasible net production, zero aggregate internal exchange, equality of aggregate imports and exports to their respective individual totals, and nonnegative individual imports and exports. Scope: Community dispatch exchange problem (1), including its external import and export balances.","expression":"s.t. p_j + q_j + α_j − β_j = 0, j = 1, …, n;  Σ_{j=1}^{n} q_j = 0;  Σ_{j=1}^{n} α_j = q_imp;  Σ_{j=1}^{n} β_j = q_exp;  p_j ∈ P_j, j = 1, …, n;  α_j, β_j ≥ 0, j = 1, …, n","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R001-X001","v141-c-R001-X002","v141-c-R001-X003","v141-c-R001-X004","v141-c-R001-X005","v141-c-R001-X006"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R001-P001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C004","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Every agent must reveal its utility curves in the central optimization problem. Scope: Centralized optimization formulation of community clearing. Condition: The central optimization formulation is used.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E17"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C005","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The community market is cleared over 24 hours in a single optimization problem because of the daily consumption constraint. Scope: The paper's simulated energy collective with fixed cumulative daily consumption. Condition: Each prosumer's cumulative daily energy consumption is fixed to match the reference dataset.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e21"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E09","location":{"location_id":"src-dfa28329fc-p03-c1r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":"3996","section":"II. Energy Collectives and Their Operational Framework","anchor_text":"as the solution of the exchange problem ad n of min fj(pj, qj, αj, βj) + g(qimp, qexp, ϑ) (1a) ap Γ ","equation_id":"(1)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The optimal community dispatch is then obtained as the solution of the exchange problem: min_{Gamma} sum_{j=1}^{n} f_j(p_j, q_j, alpha_j, beta_j) + g(q_imp, q_exp, theta)   (1a)  s.t. p_j + q_j + alpha_j - beta_j = 0 , j = 1, . . . , n   (1b)  sum_{j=1}^{n} q_j = 0   (1c)  sum_{j=1}^{n} alpha_j = q_imp   (1d)  sum_{j=1}^{n} beta_j = q_exp   (1e)  p_j in P_j , j = 1, . . . , n   (1f)  alpha_j, beta_j >= 0 , j = 1, . . . , n   (1g)  where Gamma = {p_j, q_j, alpha_j, beta_j} is the set of decision variables and q_imp, q_exp are continuous variables describing import and export exchanges with the system operator."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E17","location":{"location_id":"src-dfa28329fc-p03-c2r4__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":3,"printed_page":"3996","section":"II. Energy Collectives and Their Operational Framework","anchor_text":"xp) increase its own autonomy from market and system operator. les by C. Market Efﬁciency and Incent","equation_id":"(1)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The proposed market design for energy collectives ensures, by construction, market efficiency. As demonstrated in the Appendix, the Karush-Kuhn-Tucker (KKT) conditions of the optimization problem, as in (1), correspond to those of an equilibrium problem in which each agent individually minimizes its costs. This implies that both problems achieve the same optimal solution under different assumptions. Perfect competition is assumed in the equilibrium problem solution, while in the central optimization problem every agent has to reveal its utility curves. However, by decomposing the optimization problem, we are able to limit the set of information needed to grant market efficiency, enhancing the privacy level of the participants utility and cost curves as well as their preferences."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E31","location":{"location_id":"src-dfa28329fc-p05-c2r2__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":5,"printed_page":"3998","section":"IV. Distributed Optimization Approach to the Operation of Energy Collectives","anchor_text":"j j∈N3 mps This formulation allows to represent technical constraints, f g typical of power ﬂow anal","equation_id":"(1)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The nature of (1) readily suggests employing decomposition techniques to achieve optimality in a distributed fashion. More precisely, the Alternating Direction Method of Multipliers (ADMM [20]) is used here. This algorithm allows to explicitly define individual problems for each prosumer and supervise the exchange of information between the collective members and the community manager. Alternative decomposition approaches could be employed, with their advantages and caveats, as recently reviewed and compared in [21] for optimal power flow problems. Langragian Relaxation (LR) and Proximal Message Passing (PMP) are valuable alternative solving algorithms for the market structure proposed. We find that ADMM naturally fits the market structure of energy collectives, as it entails a supervisory node (not required for instance with PMP). In addition, ADMM generalizes LR, as it does not require the objective function to be smooth and differentiable, limiting the requirements to impose to the community members."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E32","location":{"location_id":"src-dfa28329fc-p05-c2r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":"3998","section":"IV. Distributed Optimization Approach to the Operation of Energy Collectives","anchor_text":"In order to decompose the community economic dispatch ﬁg- with ADMM, we rewrite (1) in terms of (3).","equation_id":"(13)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In order to decompose the community economic dispatch with ADMM, we rewrite (1) in terms of (3). It follows that  min_{Gamma} sum_{j=1}^{n} f-tilde_j(p_j, q_j, alpha_j, beta_j) + g(q_imp, q_exp)   (13a)  s.t. sum_{j=1}^{n} q_j = 0   (13b)  sum_{j=1}^{n} alpha_j = q_imp   (13c)  sum_{j=1}^{n} beta_j = q_exp   (13d)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e21","location":{"location_id":"src-dfa28329fc-p07-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":7,"printed_page":"4000","section":"V. Application and Case-Studies","anchor_text":"We calculate the daily capacity of ﬂexible consumption (L ) ve and we assume that, at each hour, the","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 3","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"We calculate the daily capacity of flexible consumption (L^{*}) and we assume that, at each hour, the flexible content of each actor is twice this capacity. In this way, the electricity consumption is lower bounded by the fixed load (L) and can range within the flexibility budget according to the agent's preferences up to \\bar{L} = L + 2L^{*}, as displayed in Fig. 3 (note that in the figure the consumption is conventionally assumed negative). Finally, we fix the cumulative daily energy consumption of each prosumer to match the data of the reference dataset. This time-linking constraint implies that the energy collective market is cleared over 24 hours with a single optimization problem. As for the generation, in addition to solar production, we add synthetic data for 6 conventional generators, in order to extend our analysis to a test case with possibility of dispatchable generation. Given the small size of the collective, we assume that the community trades energy as price-taker with the wholesale market. The market prices are extracted from the Australian Energy Market Operator website."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e35","location":{"location_id":"src-dfa28329fc-p09-c1r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":9,"printed_page":"4002","section":"VI. Conclusions","anchor_text":"degree of modiﬁcation of the participants energy procurement largely depends on their available ﬂexi","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"VI. CONCLUSIONS\n\nAcknowledging the increasing installed capacity of DERs, we proposed the energy collective as a new community-based market structure, that allows prosumers to actively optimize their assets. We showed that a distributed market structure achieves optimal economic dispatch for the community and that different collective agreements, granted by a third-party node, influence the negotiation process. This supervisory node, i.e., community manager, directly impacts the prosumers in terms of energy dispatch as well as revenues and payments. We evaluated this"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E02","location":{"location_id":"src-dfa28329fc-p01-c1r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":1,"printed_page":"3994","section":"Abstract and Nomenclature","anchor_text":"Only the most important symbols of this paper are included. αj Energy imported by prosumer j. βj Ene","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-01.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Only the most important symbols of this paper are included. alpha_j Energy imported by prosumer j. beta_j Energy exported by prosumer j. delta_j Upper bound of alpha_j. gamma Penalization coefficient (the subscript identifies the specific application). lambda_j Price of energy perceived by prosumer j. lambda_DA Day-ahead market price. P_j Feasible space of p_j. R_j Feasible space of prosumer j. U_ij Feasible space of u_ij. U-upper_ij Upper bound of asset i of prosumer j. psi_ij Cost/utility function of asset i of prosumer j. rho Penalization factor of L_rho. tau Price spread between import and export price. f-tilde_j Extended cost function of prosumer j. U-lower_ij Lower bound of asset i of prosumer j. c_ij Quadratic coefficient of psi_ij. d_ij Linear coefficient of psi_ij. f_j Cost function of prosumer j. g Model of community manager. h_j Preferences and/or transaction costs of prosumer j. I_j Set of assets of prosumer j. L_rho Augmented Lagrangian. n Number of prosumers in the collective. N_j Set of members of neighbourhood j. p_j Net energy produced by prosumer j. q_j Energy imported by prosumer j from the community. q_exp Total energy exported. q_imp Total energy imported. r_k Vector of primal residuals. s_k Vector of dual residuals. u_ij Power set-point of asset i of prosumer j. v_ij Energy traded between neighbourhood i and j. y Vector of Lagrangian multipliers."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E10","location":{"location_id":"src-dfa28329fc-p03-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":"3996","section":"II. Energy Collectives and Their Operational Framework","anchor_text":"αj, βj ≥0 , j = 1, . . . , n (1g) where Γ = {pj, qj, αj, βj} is the set of decision variables and qi","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 1","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"For each prosumer we consider technical constraints (1f) and power balance (1b) between net production, p_j, and energy traded. This energy can be traded at community level (1c) and with the system operator (1d)-(1e). Hence, we describe the energy traded by each prosumer as sum of the energy exchanged within the community, q_j, and the energy each prosumer has to respectively import, alpha_j, or export, beta_j, from outside the community, as in Fig. 1."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-bidding","v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-participation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"clearing.local","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E31","quote":"We find that ADMM naturally fits the market structure of energy collectives, as it entails a supervisory node (not required for instance with PMP)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E32","quote":"In order to decompose the community economic dispatch with ADMM, we rewrite (1) in terms of (3)."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e35","quote":"This supervisory node, i.e., community manager, directly impacts the prosumers in terms of energy dispatch as well as revenues and payments."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E09","quote":"The optimal community dispatch is then obtained as the solution of the exchange problem:"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E09","quote":"s.t. p_j + q_j + alpha_j - beta_j = 0 , j = 1, . . . , n   (1b)  sum_{j=1}^{n} q_j = 0   (1c)  sum_{j=1}^{n} alpha_j = q_imp   (1d)  sum_{j=1}^{n} beta_j = q_exp   (1e)  p_j in P_j , j = 1, . . . , n   (1f)  alpha_j, beta_j >= 0 , j = 1, . . . , n   (1g)"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E17","quote":"in the central optimization problem every agent has to reveal its utility curves."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e21","quote":"Finally, we fix the cumulative daily energy consumption of each prosumer to match the data of the reference dataset. This time-linking constraint implies that the energy collective market is cleared over 24 hours with a single optimization problem."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"7a17ff12d6524ebe880b1d8e5c7d5fbc79450e7bd95eeb0a1cb97ac865349ab5","applicability":"formalized","reason":"Rule v141-c-R001 ('Local market clearing') is the community dispatch exchange problem (1) at the clearing stage. Constraint C003 enumerates exactly the feasibility conditions of (1), which are supplied by source formula v141-b-g01-E09; its constraint set (1b)-(1g) is transcribed faithfully into an explicit expression (kind corrected from procedural to mathematical; statement, role, members and evidence_ids unchanged). The decision set Gamma = {p_j, q_j, alpha_j, beta_j} of (1) and the community-level continuous variables q_imp, q_exp are declared as operational variables (X001-X006) and the fixed number of prosumers n as a parameter (P001), all bound to the existing node clearing.local (q_imp/q_exp also to coordination.local_operator via existing edge E001, since they are the ADMM community-block coupling quantities handled by the supervisory node). Constraints C001, C002, C004 and C005 are design/procedural statements (ADMM entails a supervisory node; the community manager influences members' dispatch; every agent must reveal its utility curves in the central problem; the market is cleared over 24 hours in one problem because daily consumption is fixed). The supplied evidence gives no algebraic form for these four, so they are retained as not_formalized with expression=null rather than inventing mathematics (e.g. the ADMM iteration steps (15), the daily time-linking balance, or the utility-revelation requirement are not written as equations within this rule's scoped evidence). All original C.1 phi entries, statements, roles, members and original evidence_ids are preserved and remain visible. B evidence is unreviewed in this experiment (source_status=unverified, audit not performed), so this formalization is provisional and independent source verification is still required.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R001-X001","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"p_j is a decision variable of the community clearing problem (1) (v141-b-g01-E09), i.e. a component of Gamma for the clearing stage; it appears in the per-prosumer power balance (1b) and in the technical feasibility (1f) p_j in P_j, both modelled at the local clearing function node."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R001-X002","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"q_j is a decision variable of the community clearing problem (1) (v141-b-g01-E09); it is the energy exchanged within the community and is constrained by the zero aggregate internal-exchange balance (1c) at the local clearing node."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R001-X003","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"α_j is a decision variable of the community clearing problem (1) (v141-b-g01-E09); it is the per-prosumer external import entering (1b), (1d) and the non-negativity condition (1g) of the local clearing formulation."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R001-X004","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"β_j is a decision variable of the community clearing problem (1) (v141-b-g01-E09); it is the per-prosumer external export entering (1b), (1e) and the non-negativity condition (1g) of the local clearing formulation."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R001-X005","node_ids":["clearing.local","coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R001-E001"],"rationale":"q_imp is a community-level decision variable of the clearing problem (1) (v141-b-g01-E09), defined by sum_{j=1}^{n} α_j = q_imp (1d) and describing the collective's import exchange with the system operator; in the ADMM reformulation (13c) this aggregate import balance is a coupling constraint handled by the supervisory node, matching the existing edge E001 (clearing.local requires coordination.local_operator, C001)."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R001-X006","node_ids":["clearing.local","coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R001-E001"],"rationale":"q_exp is a community-level decision variable of the clearing problem (1) (v141-b-g01-E09), defined by sum_{j=1}^{n} β_j = q_exp (1e) and describing the collective's export exchange with the system operator; the corresponding aggregate export balance (13d) is a coupling constraint handled by the supervisory node, matching the existing edge E001 (clearing.local requires coordination.local_operator, C001)."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R001-P001","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"n = number of prosumers is the fixed input that indexes the prosumers j = 1, ..., n and the sums in the clearing constraints (1b)-(1g) (v141-b-g01-E09, nomenclature v141-b-g01-E02); it is a constant of the local market clearing problem."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R001-C003","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C003 formalizes exactly the constraint set (1b)-(1g) of the community dispatch exchange problem (1) whose solution is the local market clearing; its members are exactly the frozen node clearing.local and it introduces no new node or edge."}],"revision_requests":["Independent source audit of the B evidence used here has not been performed (experimental policy: unreviewed candidates). The transcription of exchange problem (1) into C003 rests on v141-b-g01-E09 (source_status=unverified) with symbol definitions from v141-b-g01-E02; both should be re-checked against the published paper before the formalization is treated as source-verified.","No algebraic expression is supplied for C001, C002, C004 or C005. If these are expected to be formalized, the corresponding source equations are outside the evidence attached to this rule (e.g. the ADMM iteration and residual definitions (15) for C001, the KKT/utility-revelation structure for C004, and the daily time-linking energy-balance equality for C005); a precise C.1 request for those equations/evidence_ids is required before any expression is asserted.","Units of p_j, q_j, α_j, β_j, q_imp and q_exp are not stated in the attached evidence (the source only calls them 'energy' quantities per market time unit), so the unit field is left null rather than inferred; the source should be consulted if unit-typed formalization is required.","The community-manager model term g(q_imp, q_exp, theta) and its parameter/additional-variable set theta belong to the objective (1a). Because rule v141-c-R001 formalizes only the feasibility conditions enumerated in C003, theta is not declared here; if the objective is intended to be in this rule's scope, theta and g should be extracted under the objective-related rule and bound to the matching nodes."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
